        "issue": "The note's only cited source URL is dead (404), so the note's evidence no longer exists.",
        "evidence": "GET https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/backup-and-restore/ returns 404 (also 404 at /docs/v16.0/admin/backup-and-restore/). The Forgejo admin guide lists the page as \"Backups and Backup Restoration\" at /docs/latest/admin/setup/backup/, and the upgrade guide links to it as ../setup/backup/. Neither the dead URL nor the real page states a retention policy (7 daily / 4 weekly), which is the note's core claim.",
        "fix_hint": "Repoint the source (and the Sources/Further Reading link) to https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/admin/setup/backup/ and label the retention figures as this homelab's own policy, not something the Forgejo docs prescribe."
      }
    ],
    "accuracy": [],
    "scope": [],
    "structure": [],
    "overlap": [
      {
        "severity": "S4",
        "issue": "Duplicates the sibling note's subject: the target restates the prune job instead of linking to backup-pruning.md.",
        "evidence": "Target Details: \"Keep 7 daily dumps and 4 weekly dumps; older ones are removed by the prune job\" and \"Retention is not controlled by `app.ini` -- the prune step is its own job\". The sibling backup-pruning.md is entirely about that job (line 18: \"The prune job is the timer that deletes aged dumps from the NAS.\"), and both notes also share the same source URL.",
        "fix_hint": "Keep the retention-policy concept here but replace the prune-job statements with a link to ./02_Knowledge/technologies/services/forgejo/backup-pruning.md (and add it to related_docs) rather than repeating what that note covers."
      }
    ]
  },
